# Production-only Vite environment (loaded automatically by `vite build`).
#
# This app needs NO runtime secrets or API keys: it is a fully static SPA that
# self-hosts its MediaPipe WASM + model under /mediapipe and talks to no backend
# (CSP connect-src is 'self'). The camera is the only privileged API and it is
# gated by HTTPS + Permissions-Policy, not by any env flag.
#
# Documented prod flags:

# Drop Vite's dev-only warning overlay / extra checks. (Vite sets import.meta.env
# .PROD=true automatically for `build`; this is just explicit.)
VITE_APP_ENV=production

# NOTE for the human deploying:
#   The Footer GITHUB_URL (src/components/Footer.tsx) is still the placeholder
#   'https://github.com'. If you want it to point at the real repo, set it in
#   source before `railway up` — it is a compile-time string, not read from here.
#
# This file IS committed (see app/.gitignore !.env.production exception) so the
# Docker/Railway build picks it up. It contains no secrets.
